.TH VNIKEY 1 "September 2026" "VNIKey" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vnikey-wayland, vnikey-x11, vnikey-ibus \- Vietnamese input method daemons
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vnikey-wayland
[--version]

.B vnikey-x11
[--version]

.B vnikey-ibus
[--version]
.SH DESCRIPTION
VNIKey is a high-performance Vietnamese input method engine for Linux, written in Rust.
It provides three separate daemons for different display server environments:
.TP
.B vnikey-wayland
Native Wayland daemon using the zwp_input_method_v2 protocol.
.TP
.B vnikey-x11
X11 daemon using XTest and clipboard injection.
.TP
.B vnikey-ibus
IBus frontend daemon for GNOME Wayland compatibility.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The configuration file is located at \fI~/.config/vnikey/config.toml\fR.
A graphical configuration tool is available via \fBvnikey-gui\fR.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBvnikey-gui\fR(1)
